  {
    "id": "zh_A1_func_05",
    "type": "concept",
    "category": "Funciones comunicativas",
    "title": "表达喜欢和不喜欢（我喜欢 / 我不喜欢）",
    "bridge": "在西班牙语中，表达喜好时使用动词 'gustar'：'Me gusta la pizza'（字面意思是 '比萨让我喜欢'）。而在英语中，我们用 'like' 并采用主语 + like + 宾语的结构：'I like pizza'。主要区别在于西班牙语的动词 'gustar' 与宾语保持一致（me gusta la pizza, me gustan las pizzas），而英语的 'like' 则与主语保持一致（I like pizza, He likes pizza）。此外，表达不喜欢时，英语中使用 'I don't like'（对应西班牙语的 'no me gusta'）。",
    "rule": "表达喜好时：1) 肯定句：I/you/we/they like + 宾语（I like coffee）。He/she/it likes + 宾语（She likes coffee）。2) 否定句：I/you/we/they don't like（I don't like tea）。He/she/it doesn't like（He doesn't like tea）。3) 疑问句：Do you like...?（¿Te gusta...?），Does she like...?（¿Le gusta a ella...?）。4) 强调：'I like it very much'（我非常喜欢）或 'I really like it'（我真的很喜欢）。",
    "concept_examples": [
      {
        "text": "I like pizza.",
        "translation": "我喜欢比萨。",
        "phonetic": "/aɪ laɪk ˈpiːtsə/"
      },
      {
        "text": "She likes reading.",
        "translation": "她喜欢阅读。",
        "phonetic": "/ʃiː laɪks ˈriːdɪŋ/"
      },
      {
        "text": "We don't like fast food.",
        "translation": "我们不喜欢快餐。",
        "phonetic": "/wiː dəʊnt laɪk fɑːst fuːd/"
      },
      {
        "text": "Do you like music?",
        "translation": "你喜欢音乐吗？",
        "phonetic": "/duː juː laɪk ˈmjuːzɪk/"
      }
    ],
    "common_error": {
      "wrong": "I like very much pizza.",
      "correct": "I like pizza very much.",
      "correct_alt": "",
      "explanation": "在西班牙语中，副词 'mucho' 位于动词之后：'Me gusta mucho la pizza'。而在英语中，副词 'very much' 通常放在句末或宾语之后：'I like pizza very much'。将其置于动词和宾语之间是常见的错误。"
    },
    "levels": [
      {
        "level": 1,
        "label": "Affirmative with I/you/we/they",
        "translation": "I/you/we/they 的肯定句",
        "examples": [
          {
            "original": "I like chocolate.",
            "phonetic": "/aɪ laɪk ˈtʃɒkələt/",
            "translation": "我喜欢巧克力。",
            "note": "动词 'like' 使用原形。"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "level": 2,
        "label": "Affirmative with he/she/it",
        "translation": "he/she/it 的肯定句",
        "examples": [
          {
            "original": "He likes football.",
            "phonetic": "/hiː laɪks ˈfʊtbɔːl/",
            "translation": "他喜欢足球。",
            "note": "第三人称单数需加 -s。"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "level": 3,
        "label": "Negative with don't/doesn't",
        "translation": "don't/doesn't 的否定句",
        "examples": [
          {
            "original": "She doesn't like coffee.",
            "phonetic": "/ʃiː ˈdʌznt laɪk ˈkɒfi/",
            "translation": "她不喜欢咖啡。",
            "note": "使用 'doesn't' + 动词原形。"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "level": 4,
        "label": "Questions with Do/Does",
        "translation": "Do/Does 的疑问句",
        "examples": [
          {
            "original": "Do you like dogs?",
            "phonetic": "/duː juː laɪk dɒɡz/",
            "translation": "你喜欢狗吗？",
            "note": "疑问句结构为 'do' + 主语 + 动词原形。"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "conversation": {
      "vocabulary": [],
      "dialogue": []
    },
    "translations": {
      "zh": "表达喜欢和不喜欢（我喜欢 / 我不喜欢）"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "zh_A1_func_06",
    "type": "concept",
    "category": "Funciones comunicativas",
    "title": "询问并给出价格",
    "bridge": "在西班牙语中，询问价格时我们会说'¿Cuánto cuesta?'或'¿Cuánto es?'。在英语中，我们会说'How much is it?'（单数）或'How much are they?'（复数）。也可以用'How much does it cost?'（¿Cuánto cuesta?）。主要区别在于英语中询问时使用动词'to be'或动词'cost'与助动词'does'搭配。给出价格时，我们会说'It is [数字] dollars/euros'或'It costs [数字]。'",
    "rule": "询问价格时：1) 'How much is it?'（用于一个物品）或'How much are they?'（用于多个物品）。2) 'How much does it cost?'（¿Cuánto cuesta?）。3) 'How much is the T-shirt?'（¿Cuánto cuesta la camiseta?）。回答时：'It is 25 dollars'或'It costs 25 dollars'。在疑问句中，我们总是使用动词'to be'或助动词'does' + 'cost'。",
    "concept_examples": [
      {
        "text": "How much is it?",
